  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#22361\", \"PowerToys#31506\", \"PowerToys#15675\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys#22361 is the main open ticket for restoring Cascade Windows, and PowerToys#31506 was closed as a duplicate of it. PowerToys#15675 asks for a keyboard shortcut to cascade windows. The archive shows no cascade feature or fix. Add your use case, such as cascading only one app's windows, to #22361 and upvote it. In the meantime, the workaround other users describe is a FancyZones layout of overlapping zones. This makes a cascade-like arrangement. You can also turn on 'Move newly created windows to the last known zone' to stop new windows from opening in Windows' default cascade positions. PowerToys#12305 is a related request to cascade or stack the windows of an app group in a zone.\"}",
